o record the name of the video that successfully found the magnet link and its magnet link. If no magnetic link is found, fill in the blank string.\nExpected output: You need to generate a JSON, similar to {name:\'xxx \', magnet:\'xxx\', chapter:\'xxx \'}, and the result is a JSON array. The expected output is in the following format:\n```\nStep Answer: [json]\n```\n\n# Step 3:\nCall the bitcomet tool to download the file.\nExpected output: Output whether the bitcomet command was successfully called and return a JSON array\n```\nStep Answer: [json]\n```\n## Note\n1. Each animate in json should be downloaded once, and only one episode is needed for each animate.For example, if there are three elements in json, you need to call the tool to download three times.\n\n# Step 4:\nCall the tool and scan the D:\\\\animate folder to see if there are any newly added bitcomet download files.The first half of the file name for this downloaded file should be similar to the file name obtained in Step 2.\nThe file name of the newly added download file ends with ".bc!".\n__Note:__ Both the name and the number of episodes must match. If there is, you need to return the complete path of this folder. If there isn\'t a file end with ".bc!", you shouldn\'t add a familiar path to the result.\nAfter obtaining the contents of the folder, fill the file path into the JSON by comparing the JSON array from step 2.\nExpected output: Return the json format of the example below. Your output should not have the ``` symbol.\n```\n[{"name":"xxx","magnet": "xxx", "chapter":"xxx","path":"xxx", "download_failed_reason_type":0, "download_failed_reason_detail":""},\n{"name":"xxx2","magnet": "xxx2", "chapter":"xxx2","path":"xxx2", "download_failed_reason_type":0, "download_failed_reason_detail":""}]\n```\n## Note\n1. If you can\'t find the file end with ".bc!", it means you download it failed, you need to observe the result and try it again.\n2. The "download_failed_reason_type" in the result json has 3 types.\n- When the animate download successfully, the value is 0.\n- If the animation episode number cannot be found, the value is 1\n- For other cases, the value is 2. And in these cases, you can fill the "download_failed_reason_detail" field with what you think the download failed for.\n- If download successfully, the "download_failed_reason_detail" field should be empty.\n\n', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='8d2c6eaf-5937-4c57-aed3-5a20f793a6f5'), AIMessage(content='{\n    "locale": "en-US",\n    "has_enough_context": false,\n    "thought": "The user wants to search for torrent links and download anime. The steps include retrieving information from a JSON file, searching for magnet links on a webpage, downloading the files using BitComet, and scanning a folder to check for newly added download files. I will break down these steps into more detailed tasks.",\n    "title": "Anime Torrent Download Task",\n    "steps": [\n        {\n            "need_search": false,\n            "title": "Retrieve information from JSON file",\n            "description": "Call the tool to retrieve information from the file D:\\\\animate\\\\animate_storage.json, which contains a JSON string. Format the output as \'Step Answer: [json]\'.",\n            "step_type": "task_solver"\n        },\n        {\n            "need_search": true,\n            "title": "Search for magnet links",\n            "description": "For each element in the JSON array obtained from the first step, search for magnet links on the webpage https://www.comicat.org/search.php?keyword={search_name}. Use the request header {\'User - Agent\': \'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/123.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\',\'Cookie\': \'visitor_test=human\'}. Concatenate the prefix of the magnetic link with the field after \'show - \' to get the full magnet link. Consider the chapter (number of episodes) and avoid files larger than 1GB unless they are the only option. Re